  "pipeline_contract": [
    "Spotify Web API is the playlist/catalog authority and provides metadata/artwork/ISRC; no Spotify audio is downloaded.",
    "LRCLIB synced lyrics are fetched immediately after Spotify metadata and are the sole lyric transcript allowed for offset anchors; enforce the Telugu-script gate.",
    "Select and download the YT Music reference recording, select one visual YouTube video, and download audio from that exact selected video URL.",
    "MMS/CTC searches the opening LRCLIB lyric phrase independently in the YT Music reference audio and selected YouTube-video audio using overlapping windows with original-timeline timestamps.",
    "Calculate offset only from paired word-level timestamp differences using a robust median and quality/coverage/MAD rejection. No energy-envelope fallback is active.",
    "Persist both anchors, method version, offset and matched-word evidence into workspace state, vachika.db and the progressive per-song JSON before full media processing.",
    "Continue with source-provenance validation, isolated HTDemucs attempts, complete Telugu word-level LRC, whole-song 8D, hook selection, absolute-timeline Reel render and artifact validation.",
    "Use db/vachika.db as the sole active SQLite DB; db/songs.json is generated from the DB, and songs/final/<song>.json contains that song’s complete progressive processing record."
  ],
